    "id": "vented_dryer",
    "name": "Vented Dryer",
    "templateId": "electric_dryer",
    "variant": "vented",
    "description": "Canonical functional and diagnostic ontology for vented clothes dryers (electric and gas heat sources). Heat implementation (element, burner, valve, ignitor) belongs in platform overlays — canonical layer uses heat_source only.",
    "frozen": true,
    "frozenAt": "2026-09-14T03:06:00+00:00",
    "frozenRevision": "rev2",
    "frozenNote": "CG-6.4 canonical graph #2 — signed off; W8178559 compounding baseline"
  },
  "designPrinciples": [
    "The canonical graph represents functional relationships that matter to diagnosis, not every physical wire.",
    "Manufacturer and model implementations extend this graph via platform overlays — they do not replace it.",
    "Tests produce evidence; evidence changes component and hypothesis state (handled in procedure + intelligence layers).",
    "A normal measurement reduces likelihood of a failure mode but does not prove the entire component verified_good.",
    "Do not condemn a downstream component until required upstream conditions are established.",
    "Unknown information must remain unknown — never infer good or bad without evidence.",
    "heat_source is fuel-agnostic — electric element, gas burner, valve, and ignitor are overlay components.",
    "Lint filter restriction and external vent restriction are distinct diagnostic domains.",
    "Procedure branch logic and test definitions stay in service procedure seeds, not in this file."
  ],
